1
00:00:01,820 --> 00:00:06,180
The public doesn't realize it, but
there's an evil lurking in Morioh.

2
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:10,517
It's like a silent disease slowly
ravaging our town from the inside out,

3
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:13,541
and every day more and
more lives are being taken.

4
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:21,498
What's worse, these killings have
gone completely unnoticed for years.

5
00:00:21,760 --> 00:00:25,936
It's shocking to say the least, the
thought of it's downright chilling.

6
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:30,751
And we have no way of tracking down the
murderer, no matter how hard we try.

7
00:00:31,340 --> 00:00:35,520
In fact, we still don't know how
many stand users are even in Morioh.

8
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:40,619
But people aren't worried about some
silent killer coming after them.

9
00:00:40,860 --> 00:00:44,297
They're too preoccupied with
what they're having for dinner.

10
00:00:44,380 --> 00:00:48,909
Everyone is completely blind to what's
going on outside their immediate view.

11
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:56,940
How can I only have 285 yen to my name?

12
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:59,740
Best I checked, I had 20,000 in savings!

13
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:08,020
12 yen!

14
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:12,420
I've got to work on my spending habits.

15
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:16,211
That 20,000 yen was for those
dope designer shoes I wanted.

16
00:01:16,760 --> 00:01:20,017
What the hell else could I have
spent that amount of money on?

17
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:22,218
This is that crusty old man's fault!

18
00:01:22,360 --> 00:01:23,937
He charged a hundred and thirty thousand

19
00:01:24,020 --> 00:01:26,317
yen to my cart when he
bought that baby shit!

20
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:29,477
Though I have to admit the
geezer paid me back in full.

21
00:01:29,560 --> 00:01:31,797
After that I got bit by
a mysterious spending

22
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:34,762
bug and my money sense
flew right out the window!

23
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:38,317
Maybe I'll get lucky and find a
thousand yen laying around somewhere,

24
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:40,812
though the odds of that are slim to none!

25
00:01:52,060 --> 00:01:53,780
It's a disgusting roach.

26
00:01:54,020 --> 00:01:56,961
That's a health code
violation if I ever seen one.

27
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:03,880
Is that a stand?

28
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:05,810
Great.

29
00:02:05,893 --> 00:02:07,140
I got one man.

30
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:15,022
Where do you think you're going?

31
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:20,160
I was right, it's a stand!

32
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:23,579
Just when I thought this
day couldn't get any worse.

33
00:02:54,100 --> 00:02:58,280
I don't know.

34
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:46,997
I don't know what I'm saying.

35
00:03:47,080 --> 00:03:48,720
Where the hell is it going?

36
00:03:50,260 --> 00:03:51,480
There's another one.

37
00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:54,220
Dammit, what the hell are you?

38
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:57,327
You're about to get
slaughtered, you hear me?

39
00:03:59,260 --> 00:04:00,090
Okuyasu!

40
00:04:00,173 --> 00:04:01,360
Oh, heyya, Josuke.

41
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:03,237
Look, there's an enemy stand.

42
00:04:03,320 --> 00:04:05,085
I'm gonna squash him to death.

43
00:04:05,660 --> 00:04:07,200
Now there are two of them!

44
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:10,597
Yeah, I followed one of those little
pests all the way from the bank.

45
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:12,897
How did the one you're after attack you?

46
00:04:12,980 --> 00:04:15,480
Well, he didn't actually attack me.

47
00:04:15,980 --> 00:04:19,037
I was trying to buy a bottle
of Calpis water when suddenly

48
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:21,837
it popped out from under the
vending machine and took off!

49
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:22,750
That's all?

50
00:04:22,833 --> 00:04:24,657
You mean it didn't try
to pick a fight with you?

51
00:04:24,740 --> 00:04:27,377
Then why were you ranting about
wanting to squash it to death?

52
00:04:27,460 --> 00:04:29,537
Cause the stupid little
bastard startled me so

53
00:04:29,620 --> 00:04:32,317
bad I spilled the damn
water all over my uniform!

54
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:35,480
I want my money back, damn it! I got one!

55
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:37,080
Check it out!

56
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:39,477
Looks like another one of
those things joined the pack!

57
00:04:42,640 --> 00:04:43,470
Whoa!

58
00:04:43,553 --> 00:04:44,977
What the hell are these things?

59
00:04:45,060 --> 00:04:46,357
There are so many of them!

60
00:04:46,440 --> 00:04:48,264
They're like a pint-sized army!

61
00:04:48,540 --> 00:04:50,757
Okuyasu, try not to
take this the wrong way,

62
00:04:50,840 --> 00:04:53,077
but they kind of remind me
of your brother's stance.

63
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:57,677
Although, the fact that they're completely
ignoring us is giving me a bad feeling.

64
00:04:57,760 --> 00:05:00,360
It's really creepy if you ask me. Yeah.

65
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:09,620
Stay alert.

66
00:05:09,820 --> 00:05:11,817
The user is probably somewhere nearby.

67
00:05:11,900 --> 00:05:12,730
Focus.

68
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:25,030
What?

69
00:05:25,460 --> 00:05:26,290
It's money!

70
00:05:26,373 --> 00:05:30,535
Oh, that's right, it took a one yen
coin from under the ATM at the bank.

71
00:05:31,060 --> 00:05:35,119
As crazy as it is, I'm pretty sure
all those coins are the real deal.

72
00:05:35,700 --> 00:05:36,935
Great work, everyone.

73
00:05:37,140 --> 00:05:38,846
These are some good pickings.

74
00:05:39,180 --> 00:05:41,920
Like they say, a yen
saved is a yen earned.

75
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:45,962
And counting all the money that
we've saved, this makes 5,000 yen.

76
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:52,757
As long as I have you by my side harvest,
I'll have everything I need to get by.

77
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:54,177
for the rest of my life.

78
00:05:54,260 --> 00:05:56,677
Hey, do you see the way
he's talking to that stand.

79
00:05:56,760 --> 00:05:59,237
He must be the user given
how chummy they are.

80
00:05:59,320 --> 00:06:00,150
You're right.

81
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:03,537
Looks like another sorry chump
got tagged by the bow and arrow.

82
00:06:03,620 --> 00:06:08,208
But going by his goofy attitude, it
doesn't seem like he wants to hurt anyone.

83
00:06:16,860 --> 00:06:17,690
Grin.

84
00:06:19,460 --> 00:06:21,357
Oh wow, this is so neat.

85
00:06:21,440 --> 00:06:24,499
I had no clue other people
could see my harvest too.

86
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:31,940
Hey, guys, you can
really see it, can't you?

87
00:06:32,160 --> 00:06:35,080
Yeah, so you know, they're
called stands. Wow.

88
00:06:35,940 --> 00:06:40,040
I'm Josuke Higashikata, and
this here is Okuyasu Nijimura.

89
00:06:40,740 --> 00:06:43,620
This means we're friends,
my very first friends!

90
00:06:43,960 --> 00:06:44,960
Oh, right.

91
00:06:45,200 --> 00:06:48,553
I guess I should tell you that
my name is Shigeki Oyangu.

92
00:06:48,740 --> 00:06:51,257
I'm an eighth grader at
Burugaoka Middle School.

93
00:06:51,340 --> 00:06:55,177
I weigh 110 kilograms and
my mommy and daddy call

94
00:06:55,260 --> 00:06:57,817
me Shigechi because I'm
their special little man.

95
00:06:57,900 --> 00:07:00,697
First they called me little
Shige, but now it's Shigechi.

96
00:07:00,780 --> 00:07:03,545
I also have a pet turtle
and his name is Kinoto.

97
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:06,957
I was home the other
day and all of a sudden

98
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:08,977
I had the urge to find out whether the 41,

99
00:07:09,060 --> 00:07:12,020
62, and 150 yen stamps tasted the same.

100
00:07:12,180 --> 00:07:16,057
So I started licking them all over and
my mommy yelled at me something fierce.

101
00:07:16,140 --> 00:07:19,297
This is a picture of my mommy,
the one who yelled at me.

102
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:20,257
A picture?

103
00:07:20,340 --> 00:07:23,497
Holy shit, your mom is actually
pretty easy on the eyes.

104
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:24,410
What the hell?

105
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:26,020
So, uh, question for you.

106
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:28,674
These things are called Harvest, right?

107
00:07:28,760 --> 00:07:31,717
Were they really the ones who
picked up all these coins?

108
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:32,857
You bet they were.

109
00:07:32,940 --> 00:07:35,497
They got them from ditches in
the bottom of vending machines,

110
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:37,657
but I'm not a robber if
that's what you're thinking.

111
00:07:37,740 --> 00:07:40,317
I already talked to the
Koban policeman about it.

112
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:44,617
He said it wasn't necessary to return
coin denominations less than 100 yen.

113
00:07:44,700 --> 00:07:47,057
Nothing pees me off more
than doing bad things.

114
00:07:47,140 --> 00:07:49,737
I don't think there's anything
bad about what you're doing.

115
00:07:49,820 --> 00:07:52,537
If you ask me, you're
doing society a big favor.

116
00:07:52,620 --> 00:07:53,957
It's no boatload of cash,

117
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:57,737
but you're taking forgotten funds and
putting them back into the Japanese economy.

118
00:07:57,820 --> 00:07:59,526
You're doing great work here.

119
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:03,070
Really?

120
00:08:03,153 --> 00:08:03,983
Do you mean it?

121
00:08:04,066 --> 00:08:04,896
You think it's great?

122
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:07,757
Does that mean you think I'm great too?

123
00:08:07,840 --> 00:08:08,670
Be honest.

124
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:11,805
Oh man, talk about being
hidden in plain sight.

125
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:13,677
I've got to hand it to the guy.

126
00:08:13,760 --> 00:08:16,477
No one would ever think of
collecting money like this.

127
00:08:16,560 --> 00:08:18,120
I'm so jealous.

128
00:08:18,380 --> 00:08:19,733
He's a freakin' genius!

129
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:20,730
I...

130
00:08:20,813 --> 00:08:25,057
I may have heard you incorrectly, but did
you happen to say I was a freakin' genius?

131
00:08:25,140 --> 00:08:28,117
No one has ever said anything
like that to me before.

132
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:31,017
I've picked up 120,000
yen since I started...

133
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:32,677
120,000?!

134
00:08:32,760 --> 00:08:35,940
But your kind words make me even happier.

135
00:08:36,300 --> 00:08:39,420
Hey, you have 120,000
yen? Pretty good, huh?

136
00:08:39,740 --> 00:08:42,297
And you scrounged together
all that money around Morioh?

137
00:08:42,380 --> 00:08:43,210
Yep.

138
00:08:43,293 --> 00:08:46,157
It's the only way to do things since
I never stepped foot out of town.

139
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:51,017
I could get lost and some Grip might
take advantage of my innocence, hee hee.

140
00:08:51,100 --> 00:08:51,960
No fair.

141
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:54,416
I have 12 yen and he's rolling in it.

142
00:08:57,280 --> 00:08:59,809
Aokuyasu, what's wrong
with your left foot?

143
00:09:01,300 --> 00:09:02,840
Whoa, what in the world?

144
00:09:02,980 --> 00:09:06,215
How did 350 in coins end up
hiding right under my foot?

145
00:09:06,340 --> 00:09:09,077
You think this random money
might belong to Shigekio?

146
00:09:09,160 --> 00:09:10,997
He should keep an eye on his dash.

147
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:12,200
You sneaky dick.

148
00:09:13,700 --> 00:09:14,780
Oh, here you go.

149
00:09:15,020 --> 00:09:16,117
I'll give you guys half.

150
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:17,357
Would that make you happy?

151
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:18,270
Huh?

152
00:09:18,353 --> 00:09:20,517
We're each other's bestest
friends now, right?

153
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:22,257
We can all hang out and do cool things.

154
00:09:22,340 --> 00:09:23,170
Really?

155
00:09:23,253 --> 00:09:24,083
Do you mean it?

156
00:09:24,280 --> 00:09:25,160
Lucky us!

157
00:09:27,040 --> 00:09:27,870
No, wait.

158
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:29,117
This just isn't right.

159
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:30,997
You can't just hand over
your hard-earned money

160
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:33,457
to complete strangers
like it's nothing at all.

161
00:09:33,540 --> 00:09:35,797
Okay, this time I'll put my back into it.

162
00:09:35,880 --> 00:09:37,040
Go on, take it.

163
00:09:37,240 --> 00:09:38,946
Half of all of this is yours.

164
00:09:39,100 --> 00:09:40,477
That's what friends are for, isn't it?

165
00:09:40,560 --> 00:09:43,677
Grunting and scrunching up your
face doesn't make it right!

166
00:09:43,760 --> 00:09:44,590
Let's talk!

167
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:47,557
Can you excuse us for a second, Shigechi?

168
00:09:47,640 --> 00:09:48,600
We need to chat.

169
00:09:50,060 --> 00:09:51,295
Listen to me, Josuke.

170
00:09:51,660 --> 00:09:53,317
Enough of the goody-goody shit.

171
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:56,977
If this turd boy wants to give us his
money, then who are we to turn him down?

172
00:09:57,060 --> 00:09:59,637
Sorry, buddy, but my pride
won't allow me to do that.

173
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:01,249
It's just not right, okay?

174
00:10:01,420 --> 00:10:03,477
As long as it's not some shitty disease,

175
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:06,237
I'll take whatever people are
given, so don't you judge!

176
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:07,277
All right, I get it.

177
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:08,237
I wasn't judging you.

178
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:09,150
Chill out.

179
00:10:09,233 --> 00:10:10,063
Stop crying.

180
00:10:10,146 --> 00:10:10,976
But you said...

181
00:10:11,059 --> 00:10:11,889
Look, I know how you feel.

182
00:10:11,972 --> 00:10:14,137
I'm not exactly raking
in yin myself, you know.

183
00:10:14,220 --> 00:10:15,120
But never fear!

184
00:10:15,380 --> 00:10:19,197
I just came up with a little idea
that'll put everyone's minds at ease.

185
00:10:19,280 --> 00:10:20,110
Huh?

186
00:10:20,193 --> 00:10:23,137
You really think it's possible
to make everyone happy?

187
00:10:23,220 --> 00:10:25,161
Heh, just leave everything to me!

188
00:10:34,820 --> 00:10:36,117
So, uh, Shigekyo.

189
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:38,517
Actually, uh, do you mind
if I call you Shigechi?

190
00:10:38,600 --> 00:10:39,597
Oh, I'd love that!

191
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:42,337
All right, Shigechi, we
can't take your money.

192
00:10:42,420 --> 00:10:44,877
What you were attempting
to do just now is honestly

193
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:47,637
no different than trying
to pay for our friendship.

194
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:48,550
But I...

195
00:10:48,633 --> 00:10:50,180
I wasn't trying to do that!

196
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:51,697
Don't worry, I know you weren't.

197
00:10:51,780 --> 00:10:54,817
But if you ask me, a friendship
is something you build over time.

198
00:10:54,900 --> 00:10:57,477
All I was trying to do
was make some new friends.

199
00:10:57,560 --> 00:10:58,497
Yeah, I get that.

200
00:10:58,580 --> 00:11:00,377
And I know exactly how you feel.

201
00:11:00,460 --> 00:11:02,695
We stand users have to stick together.

202
00:11:03,780 --> 00:11:04,610
And so,

203
00:11:04,800 --> 00:11:07,297
what do you say we all do a
nice round of team building and

204
00:11:07,380 --> 00:11:09,597
strengthen our friendship with
a little business venture?

205
00:11:09,680 --> 00:11:10,510
Huh?

206
00:11:11,040 --> 00:11:12,600
Business venture? Yep.

207
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:15,417
Before you know it, us three
are gonna be stinking rich.

208
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:16,480
How do I stink?

209
00:11:16,780 --> 00:11:19,360
I mean, lots of cash. Go with me here.

210
00:11:19,520 --> 00:11:23,377
There's only so much money you can make
by picking up leftover change, right?

211
00:11:23,460 --> 00:11:25,917
I know things have worked
out for you so far, but...

212
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:28,657
I have a much more lucrative
approach for harvests.

213
00:11:28,740 --> 00:11:29,570
Oh?

214
00:11:29,860 --> 00:11:32,157
You have a better plan
than picking up change?

215
00:11:32,240 --> 00:11:33,857
This idea is legal, isn't it?

216
00:11:33,940 --> 00:11:35,597
Yeah, there's nothing corrupt about it.

217
00:11:35,680 --> 00:11:37,117
And no one will get hurt in the process.

218
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:38,380
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

219
00:11:38,640 --> 00:11:41,137
I'm liking what I'm hearing,
so what's your idea?

220
00:11:41,220 --> 00:11:43,597
Well, that's where the
business part comes in.

221
00:11:43,680 --> 00:11:46,737
And as compensation for coming
up with this marvelous proposal,

222
00:11:46,820 --> 00:11:48,317
you give us half the profits.

223
00:11:48,400 --> 00:11:50,197
The other half will go to you, Shigechi.

224
00:11:50,280 --> 00:11:51,697
The three of us are
going to have to put our

225
00:11:51,780 --> 00:11:53,697
heads together if we want
to pull this thing off.

226
00:11:53,780 --> 00:11:57,097
But when all is said and done, we'll
finally get the payday we deserve.

227
00:11:57,180 --> 00:11:59,460
That sounds good, but I'm confused.

228
00:11:59,840 --> 00:12:02,217
What's my job supposed to be in all this?

229
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:04,006
Do you know what I'm holding?

230
00:12:04,420 --> 00:12:06,900
It's a blue stamp. Right.

231
00:12:07,180 --> 00:12:09,957
It comes with every 100
yen purchased from Kameyu.

232
00:12:10,040 --> 00:12:11,917
You must have heard of
a chain this famous.

233
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:14,617
It's one of Eastern Japan's
biggest department stores.

234
00:12:14,700 --> 00:12:16,597
And the best part about these stickers is

235
00:12:16,680 --> 00:12:18,977
there are plenty of
people who just toss them.

236
00:12:19,060 --> 00:12:19,890
Ooh.

237
00:12:19,973 --> 00:12:21,313
But wait, there's more.

238
00:12:21,420 --> 00:12:24,479
A 20 yen voucher from that
stationery store Meiwado.

239
00:12:24,780 --> 00:12:27,133
And here's a voucher from CD shop Oscar.

240
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:30,017
Ten will get you 2,000
yen worth of merchandise.

241
00:12:30,100 --> 00:12:31,617
Here's one from the cleaners.

242
00:12:31,700 --> 00:12:32,837
Marching Kids Toy Store.

243
00:12:32,920 --> 00:12:35,508
And this is a card from
Yotsuba Electronics.

244
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:38,017
Now pay attention,
because this is important.

245
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:41,360
With a place like Kamayu,
if you use this sticker,

246
00:12:41,560 --> 00:12:43,177
you can get a little bit of cash back.

247
00:12:43,260 --> 00:12:45,137
Oh, I see what you're getting at!

248
00:12:45,220 --> 00:12:47,280
You're as amazing as ever, Josuke!

249
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:49,795
This is the best plan I've ever heard!

250
00:12:52,320 --> 00:12:55,085
All right, everybody, go
into what you do best!

251
00:12:58,900 --> 00:13:02,197
By themselves, these things are
as worthless as scraps of paper.

252
00:13:02,280 --> 00:13:06,897
But, if you use Harvest to pick up the tens
of thousands of them lying around town,

253
00:13:06,980 --> 00:13:07,810
well,

254
00:13:07,893 --> 00:13:09,839
that's an entirely different story!

255
00:13:10,380 --> 00:13:11,210
Got it!

256
00:13:11,680 --> 00:13:12,880
This trash can!

257
00:13:13,920 --> 00:13:15,000
Now that one!

258
00:13:15,800 --> 00:13:17,280
Got it! Got it!

259
00:13:18,100 --> 00:13:19,260
Got it! Got it!

260
00:13:25,220 --> 00:13:26,050
Look!

261
00:13:26,133 --> 00:13:27,417
They just keep piling up!

262
00:13:27,500 --> 00:13:29,147
I've lost count of them all!

263
00:13:29,660 --> 00:13:31,477
Your stance the greatest ever!

264
00:13:31,560 --> 00:13:33,080
Amazing Shigechi!

265
00:13:33,960 --> 00:13:34,790
He he he he!

266
00:13:34,873 --> 00:13:35,960
Another compliment!

267
00:13:36,420 --> 00:13:39,517
A few are torn, but I'll fix
them with Shining Diamond!

268
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:40,430
Oh boy!

269
00:13:40,800 --> 00:13:42,565
We must have thousands by now!

270
00:13:42,680 --> 00:13:44,897
By the looks of it, it's
over a hundred thousand!

271
00:13:44,980 --> 00:13:45,810
Yes!

272
00:13:46,120 --> 00:13:48,473
This day belongs to the unbeatable trio!

273
00:13:48,700 --> 00:13:49,935
Now let's go cash in!

274
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:50,950
Yeah!

275
00:13:51,560 --> 00:13:54,717
So Josuke, what was that you
were saying about your pride?

276
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:58,017
You're such a smooth talker, it's
like you do this for a living!

277
00:13:58,100 --> 00:14:01,177
Everyone's gonna be so happy in
the end, man, so it's all good!

278
00:14:01,260 --> 00:14:03,640
Wow, I have friends now.

279
00:14:04,560 --> 00:14:06,089
Friendship is the coolest.

280
00:14:10,260 --> 00:14:13,060
Um, Okuyasu, I'm getting kinda nervous.

281
00:14:13,460 --> 00:14:15,437
Do you think Josuke's gonna be okay?

282
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:18,577
Turning those thingies into
money sounds really tricky.

283
00:14:18,660 --> 00:14:19,760
Relax, Shigechi.

284
00:14:19,980 --> 00:14:22,274
Give Josuke a chance to work his magic.

285
00:14:26,900 --> 00:14:30,000
It's Okuyasu and, uh, who is that?

286
00:14:31,740 --> 00:14:32,570
Okuyasu!

287
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:53,880
Hey, Josuke!

288
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:55,435
How'd it go in there?

289
00:14:55,560 --> 00:14:57,442
Did you manage to get our money?

290
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:00,117
They didn't tell you
to piss off, did they?

291
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:05,020
I found out that the CD shop and toy
store don't do cash back. That said,

292
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:09,757
we can exchange the coupons for about
40,000 yen worth of CDs and video games.

293
00:15:09,840 --> 00:15:11,477
Yeah, yeah, that doesn't matter right now.

294
00:15:11,560 --> 00:15:12,619
What about Kameyu?

295
00:15:12,740 --> 00:15:15,937
Please tell me you were able to
get cash for the Kameyu stickers.

296
00:15:16,020 --> 00:15:17,100
Not exactly.

297
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:20,080
Something unexpected came up last minute.

298
00:15:20,820 --> 00:15:22,460
S-something unexpected?

299
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:30,280
We got 61,500 yen back instead!

300
00:15:31,780 --> 00:15:33,956
Behold the genuine article, Shigechi!

301
00:15:35,240 --> 00:15:37,320
Oh boy, oh boy, it's real money!

302
00:15:37,780 --> 00:15:39,577
Real cash right before my very eyes!

303
00:15:39,660 --> 00:15:41,484
This is like a dream come true!

304
00:15:42,620 --> 00:15:44,000
You are the best!

305
00:15:44,240 --> 00:15:45,700
Your harvest is amazing!

306
00:15:45,960 --> 00:15:50,277
No other stand's ever come close to
its prowess! Really? You mean it?

307
00:15:50,360 --> 00:15:51,437
You think it's amazing?

308
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:52,520
Oh, wow.

309
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:54,237
I don't usually get compliments.

310
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:56,037
You guys have been super nice.

311
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:57,117
I don't know what to say.

312
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:59,082
Do you really think I'm amazing?

313
00:15:59,180 --> 00:16:01,597
Hey, have some faith
in yourself, Shigechi.

314
00:16:01,680 --> 00:16:04,837
Yeah, you've got a power no one
else could ever dream of having.

315
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:08,980
You keep talking like that, and
I'll be a sobbing mess. All right.

316
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:12,224
Hey, doll face, I got a
fat stack of greenbacks.

317
00:16:12,340 --> 00:16:13,170
Wanna have some fun?

318
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:23,790
Oh, yeah.

319
00:16:23,873 --> 00:16:26,057
Okuyasu Josuke, I've
got something for you.

320
00:16:26,140 --> 00:16:28,080
This is your cut, 10,000 large.

321
00:16:34,020 --> 00:16:36,726
Hey, Shigechi, what the
hell is going on here?

322
00:16:39,080 --> 00:16:42,417
The three of us are comrades in
business and life, aren't we?

323
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:44,457
I mean, you'd say that
we were friends, right?

324
00:16:44,540 --> 00:16:45,477
Yeah, of course.

325
00:16:45,560 --> 00:16:46,390
We're a team.

326
00:16:46,700 --> 00:16:51,053
Well, the money I've gifted you is a
generous token of our new friendship.

327
00:16:51,900 --> 00:16:53,040
Hold up a sec!

328
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:55,737
This isn't the amount
we agreed on, Shigechi!

329
00:16:55,820 --> 00:16:59,857
You promised us that we'd get half of
whatever money we managed to scrape together!

330
00:16:59,940 --> 00:17:03,640
Half of 61,500 yen is 30,750!

331
00:17:04,420 --> 00:17:05,740
Really, I said that?

332
00:17:06,040 --> 00:17:07,937
Nothing you're saying rings any bells!

333
00:17:08,020 --> 00:17:08,850
Say what?!

334
00:17:08,933 --> 00:17:10,440
Besides, it's not fair!

335
00:17:10,660 --> 00:17:12,057
My harvest did all the work!

336
00:17:12,140 --> 00:17:15,417
I don't remember you guys lifting
a single finger to help out!

337
00:17:15,500 --> 00:17:16,676
The work was all me!

338
00:17:16,920 --> 00:17:20,597
Maybe you two don't realize it,
but you're all talking no action!

339
00:17:20,680 --> 00:17:22,060
Shut your damn mouth!

340
00:17:22,460 --> 00:17:25,037
If Josuke hadn't come up with
the idea in the first place,

341
00:17:25,120 --> 00:17:27,797
you never would have thought of
picking up those stupid stickers!

342
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,917
Now I would have come
up with it eventually.

343
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:32,059
I'm the amazing Shigechi, remember?

344
00:17:32,420 --> 00:17:33,250
Wrong!

345
00:17:33,333 --> 00:17:37,985
There's no way a cantaloupe head like you
would have thought of a plan like that!

346
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:39,200
Stop, Okuyasu!

347
00:17:39,640 --> 00:17:42,120
Don't do something you'll regret later!

348
00:17:43,780 --> 00:17:44,660
Just great.

349
00:17:44,880 --> 00:17:46,357
The band's broken up already.

350
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:48,197
He was happy to give us a few thousand.

351
00:17:48,280 --> 00:17:50,637
But the moment we ask
for a few ten thousands

352
00:17:50,720 --> 00:17:53,602
now we're stepping over
the line all of a sudden.

353
00:17:55,020 --> 00:17:56,797
He really doesn't mean any harm.

354
00:17:56,880 --> 00:18:00,417
He just has the mentality of
a little kid no matter what we

355
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:03,417
say it's gonna feel like we're
duping him out of his money?

356
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:07,057
It sucks royally, but we should be
the adults here and call it a day.

357
00:18:07,140 --> 00:18:10,657
We already got ten grand out
of it That's enough to get by

358
00:18:10,740 --> 00:18:14,093
I guess if you put it that
way leaving is the best option

359
00:18:14,580 --> 00:18:17,277
But Melon Head over there
really rubs me the wrong way.

360
00:18:17,360 --> 00:18:19,657
You sure he's not
pulling a fast one on us?

361
00:18:19,740 --> 00:18:20,570
No, Okuyasu.

362
00:18:20,860 --> 00:18:22,857
And fighting's not going
to get us anywhere.

363
00:18:22,940 --> 00:18:24,617
We have to handle this delicately.

364
00:18:24,700 --> 00:18:27,818
I say we school him on how
mature adults do business.

365
00:18:28,020 --> 00:18:30,549
Sly dog, you're still
England for the cash.

366
00:18:30,700 --> 00:18:32,200
You fickle bastard, you.

367
00:18:33,620 --> 00:18:36,444
Have I ever told you I
love that brain of yours?

368
00:18:36,640 --> 00:18:37,780
You win, Shigechi.

369
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:40,529
We'll gladly accept
this amount as our cut.

370
00:18:41,600 --> 00:18:42,430
Okuyasu.

371
00:18:42,860 --> 00:18:44,497
You want something to drink?

372
00:18:44,580 --> 00:18:47,286
Pick anyone you want,
I'm rich, so it's on me.

373
00:18:47,600 --> 00:18:49,437
If you're treating, I'm drinking.

374
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:52,402
And you know, I think I
want some cowpiece water.

375
00:18:52,820 --> 00:18:53,650
Go for it.

376
00:18:57,620 --> 00:18:59,837
Josuke, how come you're
throwing those away?

377
00:18:59,920 --> 00:19:03,937
Because they're nothing but worthless junk
now, just like year-end lottery tickets.

378
00:19:04,020 --> 00:19:06,057
I remember telling
Shigechi to pick these up

379
00:19:06,140 --> 00:19:08,077
when he was grabbing
all the other tickets.

380
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:11,157
You mean these losing New
Year's postcard lottery letters?

381
00:19:11,240 --> 00:19:14,557
And just how would you know
if these were losing tickets?

382
00:19:14,640 --> 00:19:15,758
That's an easy one.

383
00:19:16,020 --> 00:19:18,537
No one's gonna throw away a
winning ticket, you dumbass.

384
00:19:18,620 --> 00:19:19,450
You say that,

385
00:19:19,533 --> 00:19:21,097
but I've heard that a lot of
people forget to check their

386
00:19:21,180 --> 00:19:24,057
numbers and then end up missing
out on claiming their prizes.

387
00:19:24,140 --> 00:19:28,897
If this wins, you have to promise me I can
take half of it for myself or wait clear.

388
00:19:28,980 --> 00:19:30,980
Fine by me, half it is.

389
00:19:31,160 --> 00:19:34,137
And if you win a sheet of stamps
instead of cold hard cash,

390
00:19:34,220 --> 00:19:35,808
I'll let you keep that too.

391
00:19:36,920 --> 00:19:37,750
Geez, Okuyasu,

392
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:40,777
I never realized how much you liked
those cheap little gambling games.

393
00:19:40,860 --> 00:19:42,400
That one's no good.

394
00:19:42,660 --> 00:19:43,780
How about this?

395
00:19:44,260 --> 00:19:46,337
I didn't really think about it before,

396
00:19:46,420 --> 00:19:50,057
but do you think I can collect lottery
prizes if I'm still in high school?

397
00:19:50,140 --> 00:19:51,737
I don't see why you couldn't.

398
00:19:51,820 --> 00:19:56,377
So long as you have your ID and name
stamp on you, it should be smooth sailing.

399
00:19:56,460 --> 00:19:59,420
SG Group 121314.

400
00:20:00,060 --> 00:20:01,480
Aw, man, that's lame.

401
00:20:01,580 --> 00:20:02,874
It's just another dud.

402
00:20:03,020 --> 00:20:05,480
Thought I had it this time. Guess not.

403
00:20:11,920 --> 00:20:15,477
Uh, SG Group 1-2-1-3-1-4.

404
00:20:15,560 --> 00:20:16,460
Hang on.

405
00:20:18,240 --> 00:20:19,460
Hey, question.

406
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:24,237
If I happened to win the lottery by chance,
would I have to take it to the police?

407
00:20:24,320 --> 00:20:25,150
You idiot.

408
00:20:25,360 --> 00:20:27,057
Why would you turn it into them?

409
00:20:27,140 --> 00:20:29,237
Harvest only picked up
what people threw away.

410
00:20:29,320 --> 00:20:30,297
It's not stealing.

411
00:20:30,380 --> 00:20:33,537
And besides that, unless you
were to somehow magically win,

412
00:20:33,620 --> 00:20:35,077
it's a moot point, right?

413
00:20:35,160 --> 00:20:36,340
But best of luck.

414
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:37,830
What?

415
00:20:37,913 --> 00:20:40,940
This is SG Group 1, 2, 1, 3, 1, 4! Huh?

416
00:20:42,460 --> 00:20:44,760
SG Group 1, 2, 1, 3, 1, 4?

417
00:20:45,440 --> 00:20:48,180
It's SG Group 1, 2, 1, 3, 1, 4!

418
00:20:48,780 --> 00:20:51,839
Whoa there, what are you
getting so worked up about?

419
00:20:54,740 --> 00:20:55,580
Five million!

420
00:20:56,820 --> 00:20:58,860
There's no doubt about it, I won!

421
00:21:00,440 --> 00:21:01,737
Wait, are you kidding me?

422
00:21:01,820 --> 00:21:03,761
This better not be a stupid joke.

423
00:21:06,800 --> 00:21:07,640
That's great!

424
00:21:10,160 --> 00:21:12,860
Oh yeah! Dream come true! Incredible!

425
00:21:13,420 --> 00:21:16,361
We're the first to ever
experience this greatness!

426
00:21:17,440 --> 00:21:18,597
Don't get ahead of yourself.

427
00:21:18,680 --> 00:21:19,510
Settle down.

428
00:21:20,100 --> 00:21:22,877
Let's just double check to
make sure you actually won.

429
00:21:22,960 --> 00:21:26,820
SG Group 121314, prize 5 million yen.

430
00:21:26,980 --> 00:21:27,957
Well, there you go.

431
00:21:28,040 --> 00:21:30,158
It's hard to believe, but it's true.

432
00:21:30,260 --> 00:21:32,777
If you hadn't found this
lottery ticket when you did,

433
00:21:32,860 --> 00:21:34,637
it would have been off to the incinerator.

434
00:21:34,720 --> 00:21:36,860
Look, it expires in a few days.

435
00:21:37,120 --> 00:21:38,417
We have to get this to the bank.

436
00:21:38,500 --> 00:21:40,237
And if they ask us a bunch of questions,

437
00:21:40,320 --> 00:21:41,977
we'll tell them we bought
it fair and square.

438
00:21:42,060 --> 00:21:44,237
and hope they believe us
so we can get the cash.

439
00:21:44,320 --> 00:21:46,520
You good on that plan? You know it.

440
00:21:46,720 --> 00:21:48,014
Lie and get the dough.

441
00:21:48,540 --> 00:21:51,481
All right, we're going to
be 5 million yen richer!

442
00:21:52,360 --> 00:21:54,066
Now, what should I buy first?

443
00:21:54,240 --> 00:21:56,237
I know, I'll get some sick Italian shoes.

444
00:21:56,320 --> 00:22:00,217
Then I'll buy a new designer suit
that complements my sexy physique.

445
00:22:00,300 --> 00:22:03,337
After that, it's on to Tonio's
for his most expensive dish.

446
00:22:03,420 --> 00:22:06,137
And of course, I'll have to
go someplace cool abroad.

447
00:22:06,220 --> 00:22:07,760
I'm saving all my money!

448
00:22:08,440 --> 00:22:09,270
Wow!

449
00:22:09,353 --> 00:22:10,348
Talk about playing it safe!

450
00:22:13,700 --> 00:22:18,020
My harvest did all the heavy lifting
while those two goofed around.

451
00:22:18,480 --> 00:22:21,820
Every last yen of that
five million belongs to me.

452
00:22:22,140 --> 00:22:24,320
I won't let them take it.

453
00:23:04,173 --> 00:23:07,517
To the arms and the lips and the face of
the humic and the ball that I need to,

454
00:23:07,600 --> 00:23:08,430
I want to.

455
00:23:08,513 --> 00:23:10,197
Come and stand a little bit closer!

456
00:23:10,280 --> 00:23:12,477
Breathe in and get a bit higher!

457
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:16,937
You'll never know what
hit you when I get to you!

458
00:23:17,020 --> 00:23:21,300
Ooh, I want you, I don't
know if I need you?

459
00:23:21,960 --> 00:23:24,240
Ooh, I want you!

460
00:23:26,600 --> 00:23:30,237
Ooh, I want you, I don't
know if I need you?

461
00:23:30,320 --> 00:23:33,560
Ooh, I've got to find out.
